// №948 boundary pin B12 (the value-label second line) — FLIPPED by №952.
// The static lattice refuses this shape the same way B1 does; №952 pins
// the SECOND line: when the static gate is silenced entirely
// (METALOGOS_STATIC_LABEL_GATE_OFF=1, the test-only flag), the EXECUTING
// backend still refuses — the label rides the value through the pattern
// return (the live runtime summary), the binding sites and the kv
// sidecar, and the sink dispatcher checks it with the SAME clearance rule
// the static gate applies (semantic::clearance_failure — one rule, two
// lanes). The executable proof: tests/naryad_952_value_labels.rs (14
// tests, BOTH backends: the static-off probes b1/b2/b5/b6/b8, the dynamic
// kv round-trip, the A2 sanitizer rule, and the literal-stays-green
// control).
pattern G(x: String) -> String { return env("SP") }
pattern P(x: String) -> String { print(G("a")) return "ok" }
flow Main { input: String = "x" -> P -> output }
